+## S2: SWAR fingerprint match in the overflow scan (S-M)
+
+Status: done. **Verdict: not adopted** (rule 2 fails: LabTouchOverflowLive −4.0%, bar −10%; LabCountOverflowLive −15.3% and heavy16x ≥ 1.05 in 5/6 pairs hold).
+
+Change: in `ghost.estimate`, each non-empty word's three entries are matched against the key's fingerprint at once: x = (word XOR fp replicated into the three fingerprint fields) AND the three fields' mask; adding 0x3FFF to each 14-bit field carries into the bit above it (bits 21, 42, 63, all masked to 0) exactly when the field is non-zero, so `^(x + L) & C` has one bit per matching lane, with no false matches (exact: the fields are 14 bits with 7 masked bits between them, and 0x3FFF + 0x3FFF < 2^15, so no carry crosses lanes). Word 0's first lane holds the floors and is left out. Age and count are decoded only for matching lanes. A test checks the new scan against the old one on random and edge-case buckets.
+
+Measurement: the stock CountOverflowLive and TouchOverflowLive hash their keys with `f.HashUint64`, whose seed is random per process, so their setups and keys differ between the n1 and n2 processes (per-function setup terms come out negative). Judged on lab copies with deterministic keys (`mix64`) and Capacity 1<<16: `BenchmarkLabCountOverflowLive`, `BenchmarkLabTouchOverflowLive` (`speed-s2-labbench.patch`, both arms). The stock ones are reported.
+
+Decision rule:
+1. Answers identical: the gates pass with no diff; the new test passes.
+2. LabCountOverflowLive and LabTouchOverflowLive Ir/op each at least 10% lower than HEAD.
+3. Floods: heavy16x B/A ≥ 1.05 in at least 5 of 6 pairs. If 1 and 2 hold and 3 fails, the verdict rests on the Ir result alone (candidate, reported as an Ir-only result).
+
+### S2 results
+
+Commands: `/tmp/lab/gates.sh s2`; `go test -run TestGhostMatchExact .`; `/tmp/lab/cg.sh {heads2,s2} BenchmarkLab{Count,Touch}OverflowLive 50000 150000` (both arms with `speed-s2-labbench.patch`); `/tmp/lab/flood.sh head s2 heavy16x 6`.
+
+1. Answers identical: gates pass with no diff (sanity 62 s, digest 69 s, exact 34 s); `TestGhostMatchExact` (4 M random words plus 12 M words built from the key's fingerprint, its neighbours, all-ones and empty fields, three fingerprints each) passes. Holds.
+2. Ir/op: LabCountOverflowLive 1824.2 → 1545.7 (**−15.3%**); LabTouchOverflowLive 7271.9 → 6983.8 (**−4.0%: fails**). Per function the scan itself, `ghost.estimate`, goes 1075.0 → 788.6 Ir/op (−26.6%) in both; a touch does ~6,200 Ir/op of other work (including ~240 Ir/op in `mallocgc`: TouchAt allocates on this path), so the scan is 15% of it.
+3. heavy16x B/A: 1.280, 1.102, 1.113, 1.066, 0.943, 1.114 (A 4.11–4.74, B 4.46–5.26 Mops/s): 5/6 ≥ 1.05. Holds.
+
+What was learned: the SWAR match removes a quarter of the overflow scan's instructions, exactly (no lane is ever misread), and is the only change this round with a flood reading above 1.05 in 5 of 6 pairs; it falls short only on the touch-path bar, where the scan is a small share of a TouchAt with the overflow live. Worth a quiet-host reading of heavy16x and CountOverflowLive.
+
+Patches: `go/verify/experiments/speed-s2-ghost-swar.patch`, `speed-s2-labbench.patch`.
+
