+## S3: the overflow table's add path, word by word (S-M)
+
+Status: done. **Verdict: candidate, on the Ir result alone** (LabGhostAdd −10.9%; heavy16x ≥ 1.05 in only 1/6 pairs, so no flood gain is claimed).
+
+Change: `ghost.add` reads each bucket word once (one atomic load, not one per entry) and decodes its three entries from that load, in the same entry order (1..23), skipping a word whose entries are all empty (it counts as the bucket's first free entry if none was found yet; word 0's floor lane is left out). The CAS on a merge still compares the whole word read. S2 did not hold, so no SWAR match here.
+
+Measurement: a lab benchmark `BenchmarkLabGhostAdd` (`speed-s3-labbench.patch`, both arms) that spills histories straight into a live overflow table: a ghost table of 1,024 buckets (2 choices, 3 floors) filled first, then per op `add` of one of 65,536 histories (mix64 ids, counts 1–4, at a fixed clock): merges, free entries, and floors of the lightest when buckets are full.
+
+Decision rule:
+1. Answers identical: the gates pass with no diff.
+2. LabGhostAdd Ir/op at least 10% lower than HEAD.
+3. Floods: heavy16x B/A ≥ 1.05 in at least 5 of 6 pairs. If 1 and 2 hold and 3 fails, the verdict rests on the Ir result alone (candidate, reported as an Ir-only result).
+
+### S3 results
+
+Commands: `/tmp/lab/gates.sh s3`; `/tmp/lab/cg.sh {heads3,s3} BenchmarkLabGhostAdd 50000 150000` (both arms with `speed-s3-labbench.patch`); `/tmp/lab/flood.sh head s3 heavy16x 6`.
+
+1. Answers identical: gates pass with no diff (sanity 52 s, digest 68 s, exact 24 s). Holds.
+2. LabGhostAdd Ir/op 3275.4 → 2917.4 (**−10.9%**); D1 misses/op 0.458 → 0.457. Holds.
+3. heavy16x B/A: 1.022, 1.033, 0.932, 0.922, 0.929, 1.149 (A 3.87–4.72, B 4.13–4.53 Mops/s): 1/6 ≥ 1.05. Fails, so the result is Ir-only.
+
+What was learned: one load per word instead of one per entry, and no `k/3` per entry, saves 11% of an add's instructions; in a heavy16x flood the add is a small share of the time next to the scan (`estimate`, S2), and the flood pairs show nothing beyond noise. Order of entries, the CAS operand and the free/victim choices are unchanged, so it is exact by construction.
+
+Patches: `go/verify/experiments/speed-s3-ghost-add-words.patch`, `speed-s3-labbench.patch`.
