+## S4: victim scoring without the view (S)
+
+Status: done. **Verdict: not adopted** (rule 2 fails: CheckAndTouchMissInsert −0.08%, bar −3%; InsertSaturated −16.5% and the rest hold).
+
+Change: `mass` (go/register.go; the eviction score in claimAt and the stash's choices) answers a register that is not hot straight from word1, without building a view: with only bucket 0 filled (estimate's early case), mass = c0 if bucket 0 ends after the horizon's oldest unit, else 0; otherwise the same bucket walk as viewMass, reading each counter from word1 in place. Hot registers still go through the view. Equality is shown by a test against the old mass on 20 M random registers biased to edges (bucket boundaries, an event at now, empty registers, callers behind the last touch, every epoch offset), kept in the patch behind TF_EXP=1.
+
+Decision rule:
+1. Answers identical: the gates pass with no diff; the equality test finds no difference.
+2. InsertSaturated and CheckAndTouchMissInsert Ir/op each at least 3% lower than HEAD (cachegrind, n = 50000/150000).
+3. Nothing else higher: the library-only Ir/op (this module's functions; the runtime's background differs between binaries by up to ~1% of total Ir, see S1b's InsertSteady) of CheckAndTouchHit, InsertSteady, InsertNearFull and TouchAndCount each no more than 0.1% above HEAD.
+
+### S4 results
+
+Commands: `TF_EXP=1 go test -run '^TestMassMatchesView$' .`; `/tmp/lab/gates.sh s4`; `/tmp/lab/cg.sh {head4,s4} <Bench> 50000 150000`.
+
+1. Answers identical: gates pass with no diff (sanity 65 s, digest 64 s, exact 38 s). `TestMassMatchesView` (20 M registers: empty, bucket 0 alone, full / one-event / random counters, every epoch offset, last touches on and beside unit boundaries; clocks at the last touch, behind it, at the horizon, on unit boundaries) finds no difference, 3.0 s; with `e+1 <= oldest` mutated to `<` it fails at case 84, so it bites. Holds.
+2. Ir/op: InsertSaturated 10556.9 → 8820.3 (**−16.5%**; per function viewOf −910, duffcopy −546 (the view's copy), mass −169, duffzero −104); CheckAndTouchMissInsert 9432.0 → 9424.3 (**−0.08%: fails**): that benchmark's inserts mostly find a free or expired slot, and mass runs only when a full line picks a victim (4 Ir/op of mass on HEAD).
+3. Library-only Ir/op: CheckAndTouchHit 519.3 → 519.3 (−0.01%), InsertSteady 1756.4 → 1756.3, InsertNearFull 29296.3 → 29274.2 (−0.08%), TouchAndCount 691.3 → 691.3. Holds (totals: 522.7 → 517.7, 1834.6 → 1827.9, 29441.0 → 29407.7, 691.6 → 688.6).
+
+What was learned: on a saturated table, scoring victims costs a fifth of an insert, and most of it is building and copying the 80-byte view; reading the counters in place removes it exactly. The rule's second benchmark doesn't reach that code, so the change fails the bar as written while doing what it says where victims are scored.
