+## S5: bounds checks and inlining on the hot paths (M)
+
+Status: done. **Verdict: candidate** (four of six benchmarks 7–12% fewer instructions per op, none higher).
+
+Method: `go build -gcflags='-d=ssa/check_bce/debug=1'` and `-gcflags=-m=2` on slots.go, touch.go, register.go, hot.go, ghost.go and cuckoo.go list the bounds checks left and the hot callees that don't inline; checks on the hit, count and lookup paths are removed by hoisting lengths or masking indices, and hot callees made to inline by splitting cold paths out; a profile of the benchmarks ($LAB/cpu.pprof, never committed) shows what PGO would inline (`-m=2` with and without `-pgo`). Each removed check is confirmed in the assembly (`-gcflags=-S`).
+
+Ir/op here is the library-only figure (this module's functions, the benchmark loops included): across binaries the runtime's background work moves totals by up to ~1% (S1b, S4), more than the 0.5% this rule allows. Totals are reported beside it.
+
+Decision rule:
+1. Answers identical: the gates pass with no diff.
+2. Ir/op of CheckAndTouchHit, CheckAndTouchHitCached, TouchAndCount, VelocityCount, InsertSteady and ContainsAbsent each at most 0.5% higher than HEAD, and at least two of them 3% or more lower.
+
+### S5 results
+
+What the listings showed (Go 1.24.7): 204 bounds checks left in the package; on the hit path `slotWords` (3 checks), `find` (1 slice check), `touch` (2 on word0's index across calls). Not inlined on the hit/count path: `touch` (cost 2748), `bump` (716), `estimate` (459), `nextRegU` (404), `estimateAt` (259), `locateAt` (238), `slotWords` (125), `farAhead` (83, just over the budget of 80). Per function, a CheckAndTouchHit on HEAD is touch 238 Ir, bump 107, locateAt 71, nextRegU 51, the loop 30, slotWords 11, farAhead 11: the last two are calls that return at once (CheckAndTouchAt passes no warm slot, so slotWords(-1) answers "no"; a touch in its register's unit gets (0, false, false) from farAhead).
+
+Change (`speed-s5-bce-inline.patch`, touch.go and slots.go only):
+- touch calls slotWords for warm's slot only when there is one (`i0 >= 0`), and farAhead only when the touch is past the register's unit (`nu > lu`), the two cases where they can answer anything but their early return. (Splitting farAhead's early return into an inlinable wrapper doesn't work: a call to the out-of-line part alone costs 57 of the 80 budget; the wrapper came to 85.)
+- slotWords reads its two words through one slice (`f.words[i : i+2 : i+2]`): one slice check for the three loads. Assembly (`-gcflags=-S`): slotWords' bounds-panic sites 6 → 4.
+- estimateAt answers a register (not a hot entry) with one estimate call and no key identity: a register's estimate never fails and reads no id (viewOf needs it only for a hot entry), so the retry loop and `stashID` are skipped.
+
+PGO (profile of the six benchmarks, `-benchtime 2s`, kept at /tmp/lab/cpu.pprof, not committed): `-pgo` would inline bump, locateAt, nextRegU, nextReg, slotWords, estimate, estimateAt, count, decayStep, lookupStable, install, putNew, putOver, claim, miss, recall, relocate, mass and slotID into their hot callers; nothing here depends on it.
+
+Commands: `/tmp/lab/gates.sh s5`; `/tmp/lab/cg.sh {head5,s5} <Bench> 50000 150000`; `verify/ab.sh HEAD HEAD+verify/experiments/speed-s5-bce-inline.patch '^Benchmark(CheckAndTouchHit|TouchAndCount|VelocityCount)$' 15` (reported).
+
+1. Answers identical: gates pass with no diff (sanity 65 s, digest 70 s, exact 31 s). Holds.
+2. Ir/op, library-only (total in brackets):
+
+| Benchmark | HEAD | S5 | change |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| CheckAndTouchHit | 519.3 (520.3) | 476.3 (476.5) | **−8.3%** (−8.4%) |
+| CheckAndTouchHitCached | 563.6 (563.8) | 522.6 (522.6) | **−7.3%** (−7.3%) |
+| TouchAndCount | 691.3 (692.1) | 610.3 (610.4) | **−11.7%** (−11.8%) |
+| VelocityCount | 464.8 (465.2) | 420.8 (421.3) | **−9.5%** (−9.4%) |
+| InsertSteady | 1756.3 (1819.3) | 1724.3 (1782.3) | −1.8% (−2.0%) |
+| ContainsAbsent | 358.0 (360.4) | 358.0 (357.9) | −0.01% (−0.7%) |
+
+   None higher; four at least 3% lower. Holds.
+
+Reported (ab.sh, 15 rounds, ns/op medians): TouchAndCount 161.1 → 152.6 (0.95), CheckAndTouchHit 130.3 → 128.0 (0.98), VelocityCount 107.3 → 105.1 (0.98): inside this host's noise, in the right direction.
