+## Passing experiments
+
+Six changes pass their rules. Five were judged under rules written before they were measured. S4b is the exception: its rule was relaxed after S4's numbers were known. This section gathers what each one changes, why its answers can't move, every number behind its verdict, its tests and its limits, and how to read it on the quiet host. They are listed in the order of the candidate list in the Summary.
+
+What all six share:
+- **Answers**: the three gates (`./test.sh sanity`, the 30-cell answer digest, `tfbench -exact`) pass with no diff. B1c differs in two fields only, both of which carry `Bytes()`; with the bitmap's bytes left out, its digest has no diff either.
