+### P2. B1c: the displacement bitmap, consulted on read paths only
+
+Verdict: **candidate**. The rule was written before measuring; the experiment itself was asked for after the round. Patch `speed-b1c-dispbitmap-reads.patch`, +531/−10:
+- go/slots.go +96 (the bitmap's functions, `locateRead`)
+- go/cuckoo.go +3 (install sets the bit)
+- go/decay.go +1 (the sweep clears it)
+- go/filter.go +19/−6 (fields, allocation, Bytes, test hook)
+- go/touch.go +1/−1 (`read` uses locateRead)
+- go/filter_test.go and go/mirror_test.go (tests that plant entries or check Bytes)
+- go/disp_bitmap_test.go +216 (four tests)
+- go/verify/tla/DispBitmap.tla +172 and go/verify/tla.sh +21/−2 (the model and its runs)
+
+What it is. One bit per table line (`Filter.disp`, `(lines+63)/64` words), meaning "this line may hold a displaced entry". Displaced means an entry living in its alternate line. A **read** whose key misses its primary line reads the alternate line only if that line's bit is set, or if a clear of it may have overlapped the bit's read. Inserts keep HEAD's lookup. Memory: 32 KB per 1M slots (1M slots / 4 per line = 262,144 bits), plus 16 clear-count stripes of 64 bytes (1 KB). `Bytes()` counts both: +8,384 B (+0.22%) on tfbench's 235,296-slot filter.
+
+The protocol (B1b's, unchanged in B1c):
+- **Set before visible.** `install`, the one place an entry enters a slot (new keys, relocation copies, stash placements), sets the line's bit after the entry's word0 is in place (hidden: word1 busy) and before word1 is published.
+- **Clear under counts, with a rescan.** `sweepDisp`, after each `sweepLine`, clears a bit only if the line holds no displaced word0. It counts the clear in its stripe's `begun` before clearing, scans the line again after, sets the bit back if a displaced word0 appeared, then counts `done`.
+- **Read checks.** `mayDisp` returns true at once on a set bit. On a clear bit it reads `done`, the bit again, then `begun`, and trusts the clear bit only if begun == done.
+
+The invariant: while a published displaced entry is in a line, its bit is set or a clear of its stripe is under way. So a clear bit read with no clear around it means the line held no published displaced entry at that moment: the same answer a scan of the line would have given then.
+
+```go
+func (f *Filter) mayDisp(line uint64) bool {
+	w, b := &f.disp[line>>6], uint64(1)<<(line&63)
+	if atomic.LoadUint64(w)&b != 0 {
+		return true
+	}
+	c := &f.dispClr[line&(dispStripes-1)]
+	d := c.done.Load()
+	if atomic.LoadUint64(w)&b != 0 {
+		return true
+	}
+	return c.begun.Load() != d
+}
+
+func (f *Filter) sweepDisp(line uint64) {
+	p, b := &f.disp[line>>6], uint64(1)<<(line&63)
+	if atomic.LoadUint64(p)&b == 0 || f.holdsDisp(line) {
+		return
+	}
+	c := &f.dispClr[line&(dispStripes-1)]
+	c.begun.Add(1)
+	atomic.AndUint64(p, ^b)
+	if f.holdsDisp(line) {
+		atomic.OrUint64(p, b)
+	}
+	c.done.Add(1)
+}
+
+// cuckoo.go, install: after word0's CAS, before word1 is published
+if mine0&dispBit != 0 {
+	f.setDisp(uint64(i) / wordsPerLine)
+}
+```
+
+Why answers can't move: a skipped alternate line held no published displaced entry at the moment of the check. A read at that moment is one of the interleavings the existing read protocol already allows (lookupStable's move counts still cover entries in flight). ConstantTime's `locateBoth` and every insert path are untouched.
+
+Evidence:
+- **TLA+** `verify/tla/DispBitmap.tla`, registered in `verify/tla.sh`. Writers place, publish, abandon and take out displaced entries; sweepers clear bits; a reader looks a key up. Invariants: NoMiss (a lookup that starts after the key's entry is visible and ends before it is removed finds it) and Covered.
+  - It passes at 4 sizes: 566,029 / 10,156,426 / 2,668,777 / 14,881,571 distinct states, with writers {K} or {K, X} and 1 or 2 sweepers.
+  - NeverCleared, NeverSkipped and NeverRaced are all reached, so clears, skips and raced reads all happen in the model.
+  - noSetBefore, noSeq and noRescan each violate NoMiss.
+- **Tests:**
+  - `TestDispBitsCoverDisplaced`: after fills to 50–120% and a sweep, every line holding a displaced entry has its bit.
+  - `TestDispClearRacingPlacement`: a deterministic race inside a clear's window. It fails through ContainsAt when the sequence check is removed.
+  - `TestDispBitmapSweepRace`: 4 readers, a sweeper, fills to 80%, 20 churn batches, then a fill to 98%. About 29,600 clears a run, 0 misses.
+  - `TestDispBitmapSkipRate` (TF_EXP=1).
+  - mirror_test.go plants a displaced entry, so it now sets that line's bit. TestMemoryOnFirstUse now expects Bytes() = table + bitmap + counters.
+- **Concurrency:** `-race -count=20` passes (2 m 54 s; a first attempt hit go test's 10-minute default while the host was loaded). `replay.sh stress 300` gives 0/300 for each of the four racy regression tests.
+
+Numbers:
+- Skip rate with 1M absent keys: 92.3% / **51.3%** / 41.7% / 33.0% at 50 / 85 / 90 / 94% load.
+- LL misses/op on LabContainsAbsentBig (`speed-b1-labbench.patch`, a Capacity-4M table of ~75 MiB, past the 32 MiB simulated LLC): 1.150 → 0.830 (**−27.8%**).
+- Ir/op, library-only (total in brackets):
