+What it is. `mass` scores eviction victims in `claimAt` and the stash's choices. For a register (as opposed to a hot entry) it now reads the counters straight from word1 instead of building and copying the 80-byte `view`. With only bucket 0 filled (estimate's early case), mass is c0 if bucket 0 ends after the horizon's oldest unit, else 0. Otherwise it walks the buckets exactly as `viewMass` does, reading each counter in place. Hot entries still go through the view.
+
+```go
+reg := w1 & regMask
+if reg == 0 {
+	return 0
+}
+e := regEpoch(w1, f.unitOf(last))
+oldest := int64(now-min(now, f.horizon)) / int64(f.unit) // as viewMass
+if e+1 <= oldest {
+	return 0
+}
+if reg>>bucketBits0 == 0 {
+	return reg
+}
+n, top := reg&(1<<bucketBits0-1), bucketStart(e, 0)
+for j := 1; j < nBuckets && top > oldest; j++ {
+	n += reg >> bucketShift[j] & (1<<bucketBits[j] - 1)
+	top = bucketStart(e, j)
+}
+return n
+```
